  bootwright / context delete
      Permanently delete a context and its verified local files with --purge=true. --yes skips
      ordinary confirmation. A context that still owns realized objects refuses deletion:
      remove them with bootwright destroy first, or abandon them with --allow-orphans. Over
      lifecycle evidence it cannot read, --allow-orphans abandons the context, whose objects
      cannot be listed; a live lease refuses either way.

  Usage
    bootwright context delete [flags]

  Command flags
      --allow-orphans  Delete although the context still owns realized objects
      --name           Select the exact object name (required)
      --purge          Acknowledge permanent context data deletion
      --yes            Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.

  Examples
    bootwright context delete --name lab --purge
